  "term": "continuous panel",
  "definition": "A continuous panel is an ongoing survey approach that follows data from the same panel of users over time rather than taking a single one-time snapshot. In this source, it refers to treating online behavior as an imperfect continuous panel survey to track changes in public interest or opinion over time.",
